1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,940
Paris - 6:01 AM

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,020
Suburbs of Paris

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,920
How are you?

4
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,420
I'm fine, actually I'm great.

5
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:36,300
I know the people of France expect a lot from you in this tournament.

6
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,310
I don't want you to push yourself too hard.

7
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:41,890
I know, mom.

8
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,060
8:00 AM

9
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:49,820
Sir, the car is ready.

10
00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:55,240
Not needed today, I want to run to the stadium.

11
00:00:58,370 --> 00:01:02,660
Today we play against Japan, this is a one-on-one battle with Misaki.

12
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:05,000
We'll finally see who is better.

13
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:08,710
I will win! I swear I'll win!

14
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:13,470
The one who will wave the flag in the Paris sky,

15
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,930
is me, El Sid Pierre.

16
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:31,730
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

17
00:02:56,070 --> 00:02:58,320
Look, it's the Japan team.

18
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,530
There it is, Japan's number 10.

19
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:03,780
The one who made 5 assists against Italy.

20
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:06,330
And made 6 assists in two matches total.

21
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:08,490
The player who caught up to Pierre's 5 assists.

22
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:11,750
Japan youth's Tsubasa Ozora.

23
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:15,790
Tsubasa, about Roberto... are you okay?

24
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:20,920
Yes, I want to see him, but the match is the priority.

25
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:24,760
I was distracted during the Argentina match.

26
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:27,060
And I let them score the first goal.

27
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:32,890
Also, as captain, I must think about the team, not myself.

28
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,310
Tsubasa-kun.

29
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:40,690
I'm glad I found out that Roberto hasn't broken away from football.

30
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:45,620
He's become a youth team coach in Brazil.

31
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:48,200
And he's making his team number 1.

32
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:55,750
As long as I play football, I'm sure we'll meet again, I feel it inside.

33
00:03:58,340 --> 00:03:59,460
Pierre!

34
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:00,760
Pierre!

35
00:04:01,170 --> 00:04:03,050
Alright, that's enough!

36
00:04:03,130 --> 00:04:05,260
Ah, that's not Pierre.

37
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:07,720
Where is my Pierre?

38
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:10,010
Pierre is coming on his own.

39
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:13,480
He's not on this bus, sorry to disappoint you.

40
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,150
That's Louis Napoleon.

41
00:04:16,270 --> 00:04:18,360
France's best forward.

42
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,530
Pierre.

43
00:04:21,730 --> 00:04:26,700
As we promised, we'll settle the matter between us in this tournament, Misaki.

44
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:27,950
Yes.

45
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,580
Let it be a good match.

46
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,240
Okay.

47
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:36,210
Be gentle with us, Japan captain.

48
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:37,920
You too.

49
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:49,140
Germany     Uruguay     France     Japan

50
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:49,140
This is the first stage of the semifinals with the top four teams.

51
00:04:49,510 --> 00:04:54,350
First match: Germany youth against Uruguay youth.

52
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:01,020
Wakabayashi.

53
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,740
Why aren't you playing?

54
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:08,870
You have a match against France youth today.

55
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:11,370
I guarantee you'll lose without me.

56
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,160
Let's meet in the final.

57
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:18,500
Schneider.

58
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:21,670
He...

59
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,670
Hey, Wakashimazu.

60
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:26,130
Is he joking?

61
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,840
Does he think I can't stop that shot?

62
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,680
Uruguay - Germany

63
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,680
The match begins.

64
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:37,100
Uruguay has possession.

65
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,810
Alright, we'll win today too.

66
00:05:44,690 --> 00:05:49,820
Schester, Germany's control tower, we must not let him get the ball.

67
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:55,580
A Uruguayan defender quickly ran into open space.

68
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:58,580
They're attacking with all their might.

69
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:01,170
Nice!

70
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:04,750
Daniel-kun overlaps and crosses in front of the goal.

71
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,770
Goal!

72
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:24,230
Victorino-kun makes an overhead kick!

73
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:29,360
It only took 50 seconds.

74
00:06:29,450 --> 00:06:31,950
Germany was said to be the favorite,

75
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:33,990
but Uruguay scores the first goal.

76
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,080
We did it, Victorino!

77
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,620
Your shot was amazing!

78
00:06:40,290 --> 00:06:42,580
The candidate for top scorer of this tournament,

79
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:44,250
Ramon Victorino-kun from South America,

80
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:47,630
nicknamed the Black Panther, scored with an impressive and glorious strike.

81
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,630
It was so fast.

82
00:06:50,050 --> 00:06:52,510
I can't believe Germany conceded a goal.

83
00:07:12,410 --> 00:07:13,910
Wait, Müller.

84
00:07:14,030 --> 00:07:18,240
Just 1 goal, Schneider will make up for it.

85
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:23,120
We'll make up for it immediately.

86
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:25,670
Schneider... you...

87
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,010
This time Germany kicks off.

88
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:35,180
Hooray, we won again today.

89
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:38,310
We've won every match in this France tournament.

90
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,560
Great, well done guys.

91
00:07:42,310 --> 00:07:45,940
Congratulations Roberto, it was a good match.

92
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:47,730
Coach Barbas.

93
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:51,780
You were completely right.

94
00:07:51,990 --> 00:07:55,570
Who would have thought that Japan's number 10, Tsubasa Ozora,

95
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:59,830
was equal to our Diaz and even superior to him.

96
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:08,460
Invite Tsubasa to a professional team in Argentina?

97
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:09,670
Yes.

98
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:16,550
If he could play this well against our national treasure Juan Diaz,

99
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:20,310
I'm sure he'll also play well in Argentina.

100
00:08:20,970 --> 00:08:25,520
Also, we shouldn't let this talent go to waste.

101
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:29,440
There is a wider world than Japan.

102
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:34,950
Diaz starts his first professional league next season.

103
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:37,620
And this should be clear.

104
00:08:38,030 --> 00:08:41,490
They may be equal now, but in three years...

105
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:47,250
I see a big gap forming between their talents.

106
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:50,590
He is almost at his peak right now.

107
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:53,760
He has already stepped onto the world stage.

108
00:08:54,470 --> 00:08:55,550
Please.

109
00:08:56,050 --> 00:09:00,560
Tsubasa wants to go to Brazil and hopes you'll be his coach, Roberto.

110
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:04,520
This time, make Tsubasa's dream come true.

111
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:07,020
I want to go to Brazil and become a professional.

112
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:10,360
And then I want to make Japan number one in the world.

113
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,570
Tsubasa.

114
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:15,700
Roberto, three years ago,

115
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:18,870
why didn't you want to take this kid to Brazil?

116
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:24,200
I heard you're returning to Brazil.

117
00:09:24,290 --> 00:09:26,540
Yes, the flight is in the afternoon.

118
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:29,000
Then I guess this is a good farewell.

119
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:35,010
I want to go to the stadium and make a formal offer to Tsubasa Ozora.

120
00:09:35,970 --> 00:09:38,630
Tsubasa in Argentina?

121
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:45,770
The ball goes to Kaltz-kun from the German team.

122
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,770
I won't let you shoot!

123
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:55,400
The ball went to Schneider-kun! Kaltz-kun passed back to the young emperor!

124
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:02,660
That's it, that...

125
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:07,410
Fire Shot!

126
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,250
Goal!

127
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:21,050
Schneider-kun's Fire Shot! Known as the Fire Shot!

128
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:27,770
Germany equalized immediately.

129
00:10:28,310 --> 00:10:32,190
Only 5 minutes passed and the score is 1-1.

130
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:35,940
What kind of shot was that?

131
00:10:36,650 --> 00:10:38,280
He finally showed it.

132
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:44,370
Guys, do you know why it's called the Fire Shot?

133
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:48,710
It really catches fire.

134
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,210
What?

135
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,630
There could be friction between the air and the ball.

136
00:10:52,710 --> 00:10:55,800
Or friction between the cleats and the ball.

137
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:59,670
Maybe friction between the net and the ball.

138
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:05,600
Whatever it is, when the ball hits the net and is inside the goal, you can smell a burning scent from the ball.

139
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:11,230
That's why it's called the Fire Shot, it happens every time.

140
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:15,650
Damn it, now I have to score another goal.

141
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:19,490
This game is between me and him, a battle of forwards.

142
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:22,490
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

143
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:23,570
I could have stopped him.

144
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:31,010
Born: October 28 | Height: 168 cm | Weight: 57 kg | Blood Type: O

145
00:11:32,670 --> 00:11:35,260
The score is 1-1 and play resumes.

146
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:38,010
And Uruguay kicks off.

147
00:11:38,470 --> 00:11:43,020
The true nature of Uruguayan football is said to be "Garra Charrua".

148
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:45,140
That is, the spirit of fighting until the last moment.

149
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:49,770
But when it comes to fighting spirit, they can't beat me.

150
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,280
Bring it on, Uruguay.

151
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:54,530
Give it to me.

152
00:11:55,030 --> 00:11:56,240
Victorino.

153
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:58,740
Bring it on, Schneider.

154
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:15,300
Victorino passes back.

155
00:12:15,590 --> 00:12:18,970
Is he imitating Kaltz-kun and Schneider-kun's combination play?

156
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,780
Goal!

157
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:37,410
He answers Schneider-kun with a magnificent goal!

158
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:39,570
He's South America's Black Panther.

159
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:41,370
A second goal from Uruguay!

160
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:49,420
Did you see, Schneider? This is our fighting spirit!

161
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,720
It's going to be tough.

162
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:58,510
This time Germany kicks off.

163
00:12:58,630 --> 00:13:00,720
Will Uruguay extend the lead?

164
00:13:00,890 --> 00:13:02,720
Or will Germany equalize?

165
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:06,980
The ball is at Victorino-kun's feet, will he score his third goal?

166
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,980
Oh, there's a direct collision.

167
00:13:12,190 --> 00:13:16,280
Schneider-kun maintains his balance and wins the ball.

168
00:13:16,650 --> 00:13:18,360
D-Damn it.

169
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:28,870
Karl, do you have that much confidence in your abilities?

170
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:31,830
Mom, what do you want to do?

171
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:33,170
About what?

172
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:37,550
Don't waste the ticket your big brother sent you.

173
00:13:37,630 --> 00:13:41,390
If you're not going to work, then go support him instead of me.

174
00:13:41,470 --> 00:13:44,010
But I'm not sure they can win today's match.

175
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:45,810
Of course they'll win.

176
00:13:45,890 --> 00:13:49,230
It's impossible for my big brother to lose.

177
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,900
Schneider advances!

178
00:13:56,980 --> 00:14:00,610
Showing his powerful and masterful dribbling.

179
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:04,200
He enters Uruguay's half.

180
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,330
No one can stop him.

181
00:14:06,790 --> 00:14:07,830
I'll stop him!

182
00:14:07,910 --> 00:14:09,080
We'll do it together.

183
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:16,460
Fire Shot!

184
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:22,840
Goal!

185
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:26,100
And now the score is 2-2.

186
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:32,230
This game

187
00:14:32,310 --> 00:14:34,650
has turned into a shooting duel between Germany's young Emperor Schneider-kun

188
00:14:34,730 --> 00:14:38,780
and South America's Black Panther Victorino-kun.

189
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:42,070
Incredible, Schneider.

190
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:45,530
But that 6-1 in our first tournament match...

191
00:14:45,950 --> 00:14:49,290
I promise you, I'll make you pay for that humiliating defeat.

192
00:14:49,910 --> 00:14:53,250
And for that, we have to wait for today's France match.

193
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:57,750
I'm looking forward to our duel, Karl Heinz Schneider.

194
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:02,510
My job isn't done yet, Schneider.

195
00:15:03,510 --> 00:15:08,260
The stalemate continues, Uruguay can't concede any more goals.

196
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:13,520
Everyone except Victorino is focused on defense.

197
00:15:13,690 --> 00:15:17,070
They're relying on counterattacks with this strategy.

198
00:15:19,190 --> 00:15:20,150
Margas!

199
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,400
Nice.

200
00:15:23,570 --> 00:15:24,910
Crush him!

201
00:15:29,830 --> 00:15:33,410
South America's Black Panther Victorino-kun,

202
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:34,920
shows his quick moves

203
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,540
and his cunning!

204
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:37,590
Damn it.

205
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:47,680
A foul! Magath-kun tripped Victorino-kun to slow him down.

206
00:15:47,890 --> 00:15:49,600
An opportunity for Uruguay.

207
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:52,480
Just before the end of the first half, right in front of the goal.

208
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:55,770
And they won a free kick outside the penalty area.

209
00:15:55,850 --> 00:15:57,190
Good, we'll score from this.

210
00:15:57,980 --> 00:15:59,940
Germany rushed.

211
00:16:00,150 --> 00:16:02,320
Of course, Victorino-kun will take the shot.

212
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,950
It's no surprise Germany sets up a wall.

213
00:16:05,490 --> 00:16:09,950
The wall is useless, I'll curve it and score.

214
00:16:10,450 --> 00:16:13,450
Oh, a player substitution from Germany.

215
00:16:13,710 --> 00:16:15,960
In place of goalkeeper Stein-kun...

216
00:16:16,370 --> 00:16:18,580
Dieter Müller-kun comes in.

217
00:16:18,670 --> 00:16:20,460
He's a very tall player.

218
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,970
Close to two meters, and has a gigantic body.

219
00:16:26,510 --> 00:16:28,930
Impossible, that legendary...

220
00:16:29,010 --> 00:16:30,600
What's wrong, Wakabayashi?

221
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:33,930
Germany has someone called the legendary goalkeeper.

222
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:34,850
Legendary?

223
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:38,600
The legendary goalkeeper, Dieter Müller.

224
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:42,480
No need for a wall, it makes it harder to see the shot.

225
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:43,690
What!?

226
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:45,400
Is he serious?

227
00:16:47,990 --> 00:16:49,450
He's right.

228
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:54,660
Oh, Germany removes the wall.

229
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:58,170
Like they're going to gift the goal with both hands.

230
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,710
Bastard, he underestimated me.

231
00:17:03,050 --> 00:17:05,210
Now I'll teach you a lesson.

232
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:08,260
Victorino-kun takes an incredibly hard shot!

233
00:17:18,310 --> 00:17:24,030
Oh, he stopped it! Goalkeeper Müller caught it with one hand!

234
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,110
What?

235
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,530
Müller!

236
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:32,490
Advance!

237
00:17:35,330 --> 00:17:38,040
What a wonderful hand throw by Müller-kun!

238
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,170
Get back! Close down the goal!

239
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,670
I-Impossible, no way.

240
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:56,680
Schneider-kun crosses!

241
00:17:57,230 --> 00:18:01,690
The other forward Margas-kun goes to head it.

242
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:03,310
This goal!

243
00:18:04,270 --> 00:18:05,690
Clear it! Clear it!

244
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:08,030
The ball is cleared.

245
00:18:11,070 --> 00:18:13,950
But Schneider-kun shoots with a tackle!

246
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:16,450
Goal! Score 3-2!

247
00:18:16,790 --> 00:18:20,160
Schneider-kun's goal count is also high.

248
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:23,630
He scored a hat-trick again in three consecutive matches!

249
00:18:24,130 --> 00:18:30,220
Goal scoring in front of the net and that long-distance shot... naturally talented.

250
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:34,930
Just like me, born as a forward.

251
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:40,730
And not just him, that goalkeeper is also terrifying!

252
00:18:42,190 --> 00:18:44,060
End of the first half.

253
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:48,740
Your shot was great.

254
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:50,990
So was your save, goalkeeper.

255
00:18:51,950 --> 00:18:54,450
Wakabayashi, that goalkeeper...

256
00:18:54,530 --> 00:18:57,870
Yes, I've heard of him.

257
00:18:58,830 --> 00:19:03,960
Last year, a professional team held a camp high in the West German mountains.

258
00:19:04,630 --> 00:19:11,590
In the mountain village, a local football team played a friendly match against the professional team.

259
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:17,970
The goalkeeper was a 14-year-old boy named Müller.

260
00:19:18,310 --> 00:19:22,730
At first, the professional team took the match lightly, but everything changed.

261
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:29,070
The match only lasted 20 minutes, but the professional team shot consecutively.

262
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:32,240
But the result...

263
00:19:34,530 --> 00:19:38,660
Right, Müller was showered with shots by the professionals.

264
